      "html": "<p>Schilbe mandibularis (Günther, 1867). Family Schilbeidae. Type locality: Bossumprah River, Ghana. Maximum size 450 mm (17.7 inches) SL. IUCN Red List status: Least Concern.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1433",
      "html": "<p>Africa: from St. Paul in Liberia to the Prah River in Ghana, including the St. John, Farmington, Nipoué, Cavally, Néro, Sassandra, Boubo, Bandama, Agnébi, Comoé and Tano Rivers.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "diet",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1433",
      "html": "<p>Feeds mainly on terrestrial insects (Hymenoptera, Hemiptera, Coleoptera) washed into the water and on mayfly larvae.</p>"
